 "notes": [
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Carbon forms and uses:** diamond - jewellery, cutting, drilling and grinding tools, glass cutters; graphite - pencil 'lead', dry lubricant, electrodes, reactor moderator, Li-ion battery anodes; **coke** - fuel and **reducing agent in iron extraction**; **carbon black** (lampblack) - pigment in **paints**, inks, tyres; **activated charcoal** - adsorbs gases (**gas masks**), purification; fullerenes and **carbon nanotubes** - **electronics, nanotechnology**, drug delivery, lubricants, catalysts; graphene - electronics, composites, sensors, flexible devices."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 10,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Physics principles:** **equivalence principle** - basis of **general relativity**, used in GPS time corrections; **Doppler** principle - **red shift** of receding galaxies, Doppler ultrasound; **Huygens'** principle - every point on a wavefront is a source, explains wave propagation, reflection and refraction; **Pascal's** - hydraulic lift, syringe; Archimedes' - buoyancy; Bernoulli's - wing lift; **conservation of momentum** - **gun recoil, rocket propulsion**; **conservation of angular momentum** - an ice-skater spins faster on pulling in the arms, planetary orbits."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 1,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Formic acid** (methanoic acid) also acts as an **antibacterial preservative**; aspartame and stevia are sweeteners and fructose is a natural sugar, not preservatives."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 10,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Electrical units:** resistance - ohm; **resistivity** - **ohm-metre** (ρ = RA/l); conductance (G = 1/R) - siemens, older unit **mho**; **conductivity** (1/ρ) - **siemens per metre (S/m)**; elementary charge e = **1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C** (1 C = charge of 6.25 × 10¹⁸ electrons); **conventional current** flows from **positive to negative**, opposite to electron flow."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 2,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **More vitamins:** B7 = **biotin** (vitamin H); B-group vitamins (B1, B9 etc.) and vitamin C are **water-soluble**, while A, D, E and K are fat-soluble. **McCollum**, co-discoverer of vitamin A, also identified **vitamin D** (1922) as the anti-rickets factor in cod-liver oil."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **More polymers:** **Nylon-2-Nylon-6** = **glycine + amino caproic acid** (biodegradable); **PHBV** = **3-hydroxybutanoic acid + 3-hydroxypentanoic acid** (biodegradable); nylon-6,6 = hexamethylenediamine + adipic acid; terylene = ethylene glycol + terephthalic acid; **Buna-S** = **1,3-butadiene + styrene**; Buna-N = 1,3-butadiene + acrylonitrile."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 3,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Gland locations:** **pituitary** - at the base of the brain; **thymus** - behind the sternum, trains **T cells**; thyroid - front of the neck; adrenals - above the kidneys (adrenaline, cortisol, aldosterone); parathyroid - back (dorsal side) of the thyroid; **pineal** - in the brain (epithalamus), not on the kidney; **testes** (in the scrotum) - sperm and **testosterone**."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 3,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Blood cells:** **neutrophils** are the most abundant granulocytes (white blood cells) in human blood."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 4,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Waves and uses:** **X-rays** - medical imaging, **security scanning**; **light waves** - vision, **optical fibres**; radio waves - broadcasting; **ultrasound** - sonography, cleaning jewellery, **industrial testing (finding cracks and flaws in metals)**, SONAR (underwater detection)."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Electromagnetic induction** is used in generators, transformers, induction cooktops, **wireless charging** and the **dynamic microphone** (turns sound vibrations into electrical signals)."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 5,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **National One Health Mission:** brings together the **Health, Animal Husbandry, Environment and Science and Technology** ministries to tackle zoonoses and antimicrobial resistance."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Refrigerator cycle:** the refrigerant **absorbs heat while evaporating** inside the refrigerator and releases it at the **condenser** outside."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Osmosis:** water (solvent) moves through a semi-permeable membrane from low to high solute concentration (plant roots absorb water this way); in **reverse osmosis** pressure is applied on the **concentrated side**, leaving salts and bacteria behind (desalination, water purification)."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Bleaching powder** releases chlorine, so it is used for **water purification and bleaching**. **Disinfectants** (phenol, bleaching powder) are **toxic to living tissue**, so they are used only on objects; antiseptics (boric acid, iodoform, H2O2) are safe on living tissue."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Soap vs detergent:** soap is **biodegradable** but its alkaline solution harms silk and wool; detergents suit delicate clothes; many **older detergents** had branched chains that bacteria could not break down, so they were **non-biodegradable** and caused foam in rivers."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 10,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Convex lens** (converging): object **within F** gives a virtual, erect, magnified image (**magnifying glass**); it forms real images in a **camera, compound microscope and telescope**; a **burning glass** is a convex lens that **converges** sun rays to a point."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 1,
   "sec": 10,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Myopia** (short-sightedness): the image of a distant object forms **in front of the retina**; corrected by a **concave lens** of **negative power**."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 2,
   "sec": 0,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **SPR 1958** came during the **Second Five Year Plan** (1956-61)."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 2,
   "sec": 7,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **State Councils of S&T** (such as APCOST): frame state S&T policy, give research grants and popularise science."
  },
  {
   "book": 5,
   "row": 2,
   "sec": 5,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **INSPIRE** = **Innovation in Science Pursuit for Inspired Research**: a continuum from school awards to PhD fellowships and faculty posts."
  }
 ],
 "doubtful": []
